# Double second cousins, variant B: the fathers P1 and P2 of X and Y are double
# first cousins (a brother and sister from lineage G married a sister and brother
# from lineage H), and the mothers are unrelated. Kinship(X, Y) = 1/32, the same
# as variant A, but the condensed identity coefficients differ.
CLAS	G1	0	0	1	1
CLAS	G2	0	0	2	1
CLAS	H1	0	0	1	1
CLAS	H2	0	0	2	1
CLAS	g1	G1	G2	1	1
CLAS	g2	G1	G2	2	1
CLAS	h1	H1	H2	1	1
CLAS	h2	H1	H2	2	1
CLAS	P1	g1	h2	1	1
CLAS	P2	h1	g2	1	1
CLAS	s1	0	0	2	1
CLAS	s2	0	0	2	1
CLAS	X	P1	s1	1	2
CLAS	Y	P2	s2	2	2
